{"nodes": [{"id": "_github_workflows_e2e", "label": "e2e workflow", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately has NO push-to-main trigger: the pull_request run already tests the merge commit and release.yaml re-runs the suite at the release SHA, so a post-merge run was a third execution that across 200 runs caught nothing (10 runs, 0 failures). A twice-daily schedule (06:00/18:00 UTC) keeps drift detection at fixed cost. Full version matrix on pull_request/schedule/workflow_dispatch; newest-only under workflow_call from release.yaml (github.event_name is the caller's event, never 'workflow_call')."}, {"id": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_versions", "label": "test:e2e:versions job", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads test/e2e/versions/kubernetes-versions.json at the same resolved ref as the shards so the matrix can never drift ahead of what the code declares. Guards: supported list non-empty, sorted newest-first (release path runs supported[0])."}, {"id": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_version", "label": "test:e2e @ <version> job", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One caller leg per Kubernetes version; a `uses:` job cannot carry timeout-minutes, so the called shard workflow bounds itself (45 min per shard)."}, {"id": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_kind", "label": "test:e2e aggregator job", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Branch protection requires a check literally named \"test:e2e\" (display name, not job id). Per-version/shard checks carry suffixes and can never satisfy it, so this always()-running aggregator is green only when every shard of every version succeeded; the versions job result is checked explicitly rather than trusting skip propagation."}, {"id": "_github_workflows_e2e_kubernetes_version_matrix", "label": "Kubernetes Version Matrix from Manifest", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The committed manifest travels with the commit under test; the suite resolves each version to its digest-pinned kind node image through the same manifest. The proxy runs on clusters across the whole supported window (1.36/1.35 in production) so a PR must prove all of it."}, {"id": "test_e2e_versions_kubernetes_versions", "label": "test/e2e/versions/kubernetes-versions.json", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "_github_workflows_e2e", "target": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_versions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_github_workflows_e2e", "target": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_version", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_github_workflows_e2e", "target": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_kind", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/workflows/e2e.yaml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_github_workflows_e2e_e2e_versions", "target": "test_e2e_versions_kubernetes_versions", "relation": "share